s **`expo-dev-client`** (a custom dev build), which keeps everything you have and adds:\n- `expo-notifications` for scheduling\n- A native Android module for full-screen intent + exact alarm (either hand-written, or using a library like `notifee` which has better full-screen-alarm support than expo-notifications alone)\n- You'll need `eas build` (or local Android Studio build) since Expo Go can no longer run the app once we add native alarm code — you'll install a real APK on your device/emulator for testing.\n\nThis is a real architecture shift (medium/high effort), but it doesn't throw away any of your existing screens, state, or theme — it's additive.\n\n## Proposed step-by-step plan\n\n1. Install `expo-dev-client`, set up EAS build config (or local Android build) so you have a native dev build running on your device.\n2. Add `notifee` (best-supported library for Android full-screen alarm notifications in RN) alongside `expo-notifications` for permissions.\n3. Wire `alarm/setup.tsx` → schedule an exact alarm with `AlarmManager`-backed trigger via notifee.\n4. On trigger: show full-screen notification with a \"wake\" category → tapping/auto-launch opens `alarm/wake.tsx` (your existing screen, already built).\n5. Add persistence (AsyncStorage) so the alarm survives app restart and reschedules on device boot.\n6. Test: lock phone, wait for alarm, confirm screen auto-wakes and shows the ritual UI.\n\nWant me to start with step 1 (installing `expo-dev-client` and getting a native build running on your device/emulator)? I'll need to know if you're testing on a **physical Android device** or an **emulator**, since the build/run command differs."
