    "That confirms it. The \"Audio\" references are all UI visualizers/icons — there's no actual audio playback, notifications, or persistence anywhere. I have everything I need for a complete analysis.\n\n## Project Analysis: Morning Ritual (Gita-first MVP)\n\n### What the app is (from the blueprint)\n\"Morning Ritual\" is a Gita-first daily habit app. The blueprint's one-sentence definition: a Gita-first morning ritual app that starts with a reliable alarm, guides a short reading + breathing moment, shows today's tasks, and returns at night for reflection and tomorrow's plan.\n\nThe core loop is: **Wake → Wisdom (Gita) → Breath → Action (tasks) → Reflection (night) → Tomorrow.**\n\nThe blueprint deliberately scopes OUT astrology, multi-scripture libraries, full productivity suites, and social features for the MVP. The recommended build order is: 1) Alarm engine, 2) Gita content, 3) Morning reset/breathing, 4) Tasks, 5) Night flow, 6) Basic retention/streaks.\n\n### Tech stack (actual)\n- **Expo SDK 57** (very new — per your AGENTS.md note), Expo Router with typed routes + file-based routing, React 19.2, React Native 0.86.\n- **UI/animation**: react-native-reanimated 4.5, react-native-svg, react-native-gesture-handler, lucide-react-native icons, expo-video, expo-glass-effect.\n- **Language**: TypeScript 6, path alias `@/` → `src/`.\n- **Package manager**: bun (bun.lock present) alongside npm/package-lock.\n\n### Architecture\n```\nsrc/\n  app/                    # Expo Router screens (the 6 blueprint screens)\n    _layout.tsx           # Stack + custom floating TabBar, RitualProvider\n    index.tsx             # Home: next alarm + today's shloka + gateways\n    gita.tsx              # Shlok + meaning + listen/breathe\n    breathe.tsx           # Guided inhale/hold/exhale animation\n    today.tsx             # Task list + completion\n    night.tsx             # Reflect + memory/journal + plan tomorrow\n    alarm/setup.tsx       # Set time/tone/experience\n    alarm/wake.tsx        # \"Start my day\" / Snooze wake screen\n  components/             # ritual-ui (Screen/Header/TabBar/Diya), mascot, cards, visualizers\n  state/ritual-store.tsx  # React Context store (alarm time, tone, tasks, reflection)\n  constants/ritual-theme.ts # Day + night color system, shadows\n  hooks/                  # theme/color-scheme helpers\n```\n\nThe routing in `_layout.tsx` maps exactly to the blueprint's 6 screens plus the two alarm sub-screens. A custom floating `TabBar` (Home/Gita/Breathe/Today/Night) is rendered outside the Stack and hidden on non-tab routes and when the keyboard is open. State flows through a single `RitualProvider` context.\n\n### Implementation status vs. blueprint\n\n| Blueprint area | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6 screens + navigation | ✅ Done | All screens exist, richly styled, day/night theming |\n| Visual design (calm, premium) | ✅ Strong | Detailed diya SVG, mascot, 3D tactile cards, gradients, spectrum visualizer |\n| State store | ⚠️ In-memory only | Context with **seeded demo data**; nothing persists across restarts |\n| **Alarm engine** (build order #1) | ❌ Not real | No `expo-notifications`/scheduling. \"Alarm\" is UI + toggle state only |\n| **Audio** (3 audio moments) | ❌ Not real | No `expo-audio`/`expo-av`. `AudioSpectrumVisualizer` is a pure animation; Play/Pause just flip a boolean |\n| Gita content | ⚠️ Hardcoded | Single verse (BG 2.47) hardcoded in multiple screens; no content model/rotation |\n| Breathing | ✅ Mostly | Animated inhale/hold/exhale exists (values differ slightly from blueprint's 4/2-4/6) |\n| Tasks | ⚠️ Demo | Add/toggle works in memory; no reminders, no persistence |\n| Night reflection/journal | ⚠️ Demo | UI present; reflection seeded; not persisted |\n| Retention/streaks | ❌ Faked | \"Day 12\" / \"Day 47\" are static strings, not computed |\n\n### Key gaps to make this a functional MVP\nThe biggest gap is that **the two riskiest, highest-priority items in the blueprint's build or